            <ArticleTitle>Combination therapy with aspirin plus clopidogrel versus aspirin plus ticlopidine for prevention of subacute thrombosis after successful native coronary stenting.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>470-2, A7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We compared the combination of aspirin plus clopidrogrel (A+C) with aspirin and ticlopidine (A+T) for prevention of subacute stent thrombosis in 827 patients. At 30-day follow-up, there were trends toward increased subacute thrombosis with A+C compared with A+T (1.3% vs 0.2%, p = 0.10). These results suggest that A+C may have marginally higher subacute stent thrombosis than A+T.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
